   "body": "Fixed in my fork: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/00eb456e0b0e7ffc943e512ead8747c3c4da9061 (branch `fix/3899-gui-omp-roles-5s-locator`)\n\n**Cause.** `internal/gui/tests/omp-roles.test.cjs:132` waited for `.row.agent[data-id=\"omp\"]` under the page's own `setDefaultTimeout(5000)` (`:120`). The row is drawn only after the app's first `/api/state` read, which a machine at load ~140 answered after 5 s — hence the reporter's `locator.waitFor: Timeout 5000ms exceeded`.\n\n**Change.** That opening wait moved into `open(page)` with a 30 s bound for the cold load only; later steps, which press on an already drawn page, keep 5 s. All 16 engine/width/language combinations in the file share it. The fake gained `lateState`, so the busy machine is injected instead of retried, and a new case opens the page with the first state answer 6 s late.\n\n**Verification.** The new case failed with exactly the reported error before the change and passes after (6.8 s). The whole file is `tests 18 / pass 18 / fail 0` in Chromium and WebKit (115 s). `gofmt -l internal/gui/`, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./internal/gui/` are silent and `go test ./internal/gui/ -count=1` is `ok … 38.9 s`. The diff touches one test file and no Go code.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
